WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:07.969
By the time Jimmy Bean reached Aunt Polly's house, he was out of breath.

2
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:12.711
He was also still clutching a gardening tool.

3
00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:19.216
"I can't bring this inside!" he thought, hiding the tool behind a bush in Aunt Polly's garden.

4
00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:22.681
Then he boldly knocked on the front door.

5
00:00:22.682 --> 00:00:30.715
"I need to see Miss Polly right away," he said to Nancy when she opened the door. "It's urgent."

6
00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:35.391
Nancy found Aunt Polly in her room, writing a letter.

7
00:00:35.392 --> 00:00:41.743
"Jimmy Bean is here, and he wants to talk to you, ma'am. He says it's important."

8
00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:46.467
"Me?" Aunt Polly was clearly surprised.

9
00:00:46.468 --> 00:00:54.236
"Are you sure he didn't mean Miss Pollyanna? He may see her for a few minutes, if he likes."

10
00:00:54.237 --> 00:01:00.021
"Yes, ma'am, but he insists you're the one he needs to talk to."

11
00:01:00.022 --> 00:01:08.830
"Very well, I'll come downstairs." Aunt Polly put the letter in an envelope and rose from her chair.

12
00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:14.302
In the sitting room, she found Jimmy, who started speaking at once.

13
00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:17.456
"Ma'am, I suppose you'll think what I'm saying is dreadful.

14
00:01:17.457 --> 00:01:22.146
But I'm doing it for Pollyanna, so I hope you won't be offended.

15
00:01:22.147 --> 00:01:28.416
I'd do anything for Pollyanna—and you would too, if you thought there was a chance she could walk again.

16
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:33.270
I guess it's pride that's keeping you from asking Dr. Chilton to come."

17
00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:39.375
"What?" Aunt Polly's look of confusion quickly changed to outrage.

18
00:01:39.376 --> 00:01:44.798
Jimmy sighed. "I don't mean to make you angry.

19
00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:52.654
That's why I thought I'd begin by telling you about Pollyanna's walking again. I thought you'd listen to that."

20
00:01:52.655 --> 00:01:55.712
"Jimmy, what are you talking about?

21
00:01:55.713 --> 00:02:02.251
Start your story at the beginning, and be sure I understand everything before you continue."

22
00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:06.607
"All right." Jimmy wet his lips and started again.

23
00:02:06.608 --> 00:02:15.941
"First Dr. Chilton came to see Mr. Pendleton, and they talked in the library. Do you understand that?"

24
00:02:15.942 --> 00:02:22.382
"Yes, Jimmy." Aunt Polly's voice was rather faint. "Go on."

25
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:27.524
"Well, the window was open, and I was weeding the flowerbed underneath.

26
00:02:27.525 --> 00:02:31.009
So it was easy for me to hear what they were saying about—"

27
00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:39.565
"You mean you were eavesdropping? Oh, Jimmy, you should never sneak around, trying to overhear conversations!"

28
00:02:39.566 --> 00:02:44.086
Jimmy put his hands on his hips and stuck his chin out defiantly.

29
00:02:44.087 --> 00:02:47.782
"I wasn't sneaking around, and I'm glad I listened.

30
00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:54.917
And you will be too, when I tell you what I heard. They were talking about Pollyanna walking again!"

31
00:02:54.918 --> 00:03:01.956
"What do you mean?" Aunt Polly leaned forward, eager to hear the rest of Jimmy's story.

32
00:03:01.957 --> 00:03:07.093
"Dr. Chilton knows some doctor somewhere that he thinks can cure Pollyanna.

33
00:03:07.094 --> 00:03:15.334
Dr. Chilton needs to see her first, to be sure. But he told Mr. Pendleton you wouldn't let him in the house."

34
00:03:15.335 --> 00:03:27.153
"Oh, Jimmy, I couldn't . . . I can't!" Aunt Polly was wringing her hands helplessly. "I mean, I don't know—"

35
00:03:27.154 --> 00:03:31.146
"Exactly!" Jimmy said with a look of triumph.

36
00:03:31.147 --> 00:03:35.050
"That's why I'm here, so you will know what's going on.

37
00:03:35.051 --> 00:03:42.886
I'm not sure I have this right, but . . . Dr. Chilton said he'd offend Dr. Warren if he came here without your permission.

38
00:03:42.887 --> 00:03:47.328
And he wished somebody could make you understand how important this is.

39
00:03:47.329 --> 00:03:52.416
But neither Dr. Chilton nor Mr. Pendleton knew anybody who could do that.

40
00:03:52.417 --> 00:04:03.080
That's why I decided to do it." Jimmy took a deep breath. "So, have I made you understand?"

41
00:04:03.081 --> 00:04:12.838
"Yes, Jimmy, but who is this doctor? Is Dr. Chilton sure this man could make Pollyanna walk?"

42
00:04:12.839 --> 00:04:17.341
"All I know is he cured someone just like Pollyanna.

43
00:04:17.342 --> 00:04:20.290
Anyway, Dr. Chilton didn't seem worried about the doctor.

44
00:04:20.291 --> 00:04:29.230
You're the real problem. I mean, now do you understand why Dr. Chilton has to see Pollyanna?"

45
00:04:29.231 --> 00:04:37.465
Aunt Polly was breathing heavily, and Jimmy thought she was about to cry.

46
00:04:37.466 --> 00:04:41.872
"Yes, Jimmy, you've done an excellent job.

47
00:04:41.873 --> 00:04:50.104
Dr. Warren is upstairs now with Pollyanna, and I need to speak to him right away!"

48
00:04:50.105 --> 00:04:55.547
A minute later Dr. Warren was surprised to meet a flustered Aunt Polly in the hall.

49
00:04:55.548 --> 00:04:59.011
He was even more surprised by what she said.

50
00:04:59.012 --> 00:05:06.281
"Dr. Warren, you once asked me to allow Dr. Chilton to examine Pollyanna, and I refused."

51
00:05:06.282 --> 00:05:10.723
Miss Polly looked the doctor right in the eye.

52
00:05:10.724 --> 00:05:15.522
"Some new information has made me reconsider that decision.

53
00:05:15.523 --> 00:05:22.069
Please ask him to come as soon as possible!"

